what:
integrate (Andrew 05:37, delete v1): crates/vfs goes; span owns `FileId` (every front-end crate imports it as span::FileId or base_db::FileId already). At the flip (after ide-db is deleted: its IntMap<FileId> needs nohash's IsEnabled, which only the defining crate can implement), crates/span/src/lib.rs:34 `pub use vfs::FileId;` becomes:

    /// A source file: a dense number base-db hands out (`Files::unused_file_id`), at most `EditionedFileId::MAX_FILE_ID`.
    #[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, Ord, PartialOrd, Eq, PartialEq, Hash)]
    pub struct FileId(u32);
    impl FileId {
        const MAX: u32 = 0x7fff_ffff;
        #[inline]
        pub const fn from_raw(raw: u32) -> FileId { assert!(raw <= Self::MAX); FileId(raw) }
        #[inline]
        pub const fn index(self) -> u32 { self.0 }
    }

and crates/span/Cargo.toml drops `vfs.workspace = true`. integrate-vfs makes this edit itself in the same step as base-db's (one atomic flip) unless you refuse within two check passes.
